# Product language (no planning artefacts)

When writing **code comments**, **CLI/help strings**, **README**, **Astro docs** (`docs/content/`), **agent notes** (`.ai/docs/`), or other user/developer-facing text: use product vocabulary only.

Plans and phase trackers belong only in `.ai/specs/` (or commit-rule BAD examples). Do **not** leak them into the product surface.

## Never use

| Ban | Why |
|-----|-----|
| `Tryb A` / `Tryb B` / `tryb A` / `tryb B` | Internal dual-mode plan labels |
| `tor A` / `tor B` | Same idea in commit/plan slang |
| `Faza 0`…`Faza 13` / `Faza W` / `DoD` as status labels | Compiler roadmap phases |
| `option C`, “no Mitosis”, “formerly ww-workflow” | Decision-log / rename history |
| “leftovers”, “slice”, “tracked separately”, “deferred” as roadmap voice | Agent/plan status phrasing |
| Issue numbers as section titles (`## … (#694)`) unless the user asked for a changelog | Tracking noise |

Polish docs may use ordinary words like **tryb pracy** (mode) or **tryb ciemny** (dark mode) - that is fine. Do not invent **Tryb A/B**.

## Prefer instead

| Instead of | Write |
|------------|--------|
| Tryb A | canonical Nuxt / day-to-day Nuxt (`web/`, `admin/`) |
| Tryb B | product convert / generated shells (`web-next/`, `web-solid/`, `web-svelte/`, …) |
| Faza / DoD chatter | concrete behaviour: emit, convert, import, CI matrix |
| option C / Mitosis | custom IR / IR-first compiler |

```text
# ❌ BAD
# Tryb B product shell (Faza 13 leftover)
Scaffolded by tryb B:
option C - custom IR, no Mitosis

# ✅ GOOD
# Generated Next/Solid/Svelte product shell (product convert)
Scaffolded by product convert:
IR-first portable UI compiler (custom IR)
```

## Scope notes

- **Commits:** same ban - see `commits.mdc` (no `plan.md` / tor labels in messages).
- **`.ai/specs/`:** planning language is allowed there only.
- **Chat with the user:** may discuss plans; do not paste that jargon into repo files unless editing `.ai/specs/`.
